.TH ISOPROPYL-CLI 1 "August 2026" "ISOpropyl 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
isopropyl-cli \- authenticated terminal raw-image writer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B isopropyl-cli list
.RB [ --include-usb-hard-drives ]
.br
.B isopropyl-cli write
.I image
.B --target
.I /dev/DEVICE
.RB [ --include-usb-hard-drives ]
.RB [ --no-final-verification ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B isopropyl-cli
uses the same identity-bound raw/DD workflow and fixed PolicyKit helper as the
ISOpropyl graphical application. It accepts one exact whole-device path, never
an index or glob, and requires interactive typed confirmation before mutation.
Internal disks remain ineligible.
.PP
Run the command as a regular desktop user. It refuses to run as root.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List raw-writable removable USB and SD targets with 512-byte logical sectors.
.TP
.B write
Inspect and write one raw, compressed, sparse, or supported virtual image to
one exact target returned by the
.B list
command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --target /dev/DEVICE
Select one canonical whole-device path. Required by
.BR write .
.TP
.B --include-usb-hard-drives
Reveal or permit hot-pluggable fixed USB HDDs and SSDs for this invocation.
This requires an additional typed warning when writing.
.TP
.B --no-final-verification
Skip the final full-device hash. Mandatory pre-activation read-back still runs,
and a second typed warning is required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success, 2 invalid usage, 3 cancellation, 4 preflight failure,
5 write failure, and 6 refused confirmation. Signal cancellation may return
128 plus the signal number.
.SH SAFETY
Writing an image destroys data on the target. Prefer full verification and use
expendable media while this release is marked alpha.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR isopropyl (1)
